Generate a photorealistic, high-end product image.
The main subject is the product shown in the uploaded image and must remain completely unaltered.

The visual style must be clean, modern, and professional. 
(Adhere strictly to the Lighting and Perspective settings defined in the main prompt).

The final image aspect ratio must be ${aspectRatio}.
The output must preserve its dimensions with absolutely no empty or white areas.
Extend the scene naturally, including background, ground, lighting, and atmosphere, to fully fill the entire frame edge to edge with no borders or padding.

Strictly prohibit any text, letters, numbers, logos, symbols, or watermarks from appearing in the final image, even if they exist in the style reference.
The output must be purely visual with no typography of any kind.

Use only the number of uploaded product images and never generate additional products regardless of the reference content.

Treat each product image as a fixed visual object.
Preserve the packaging design exactly as it is, including logo, label layout, graphics, typography, and core brand colors.
Do not create new variations, SKUs, or mix details between products.

Do not alter the original body color of the product.
Printed elements on the packaging must remain exactly as they are and must never be used to recolor the product body.

When multiple products are present, maintain each product’s color independently without harmonizing or adjusting colors between them.

You may use the style reference only to influence overall color mood and global grading, as long as the product’s original design and branding remain clearly recognizable and unchanged.

All creative work must happen around the product through environment, lighting, effects, and global color grading, never by repainting or altering the packaging.

External retouching effects such as reflections, highlights, shadows, water droplets, and atmospheric effects are allowed on top of the product, but must never replace or modify its design.

Always match the product’s physical position shown in the style reference.
If the product is grounded on a surface in the reference, it must remain grounded with proper contact shadows.
Do not make the product float unless the reference explicitly shows it floating. Only secondary elements may move or float.**
    `;

