- The final image aspect ratio is set to ${aspectRatio}.
- CRITICAL: Preserve the final output dimensions with NO empty white areas.
- Extend the scene naturally (background, ground texture, atmosphere, lighting) to fill the ENTIRE frame from corner to corner.
- There must be ZERO white space, borders, or padding in the final result.
- Seamlessly integrate all subjects into this full-bleed environment.
- STRICT REQUIREMENT: The final generated image must be completely free of text, writing, logos, symbols, and watermarks. Even if the style reference contains text, IGNORE IT. The output must be purely visual pixels with no typography.
- TEXT BAN: Ensure NO letters, NO characters, and NO written language appear anywhere in the scene.
- COUNT RULE: Use ONLY the ${productImagesBase64.length} uploaded product(s). IGNORE the number of products shown in the style reference images. Do not generate extra products to match the reference style.
- PACKAGING PRESERVATION: Treat each product image as a fixed visual object. Keep every product’s packaging design exactly as it is (logo, label layout, graphics, typography, and key brand colors). Do NOT create new product variations or SKUs, and do NOT replace the printed design on the packaging. Do NOT mix details between products.
- TRUE COLOR PRESERVATION: Do NOT change or replace the product’s original body color. Always use the real color shown in the uploaded product photo as the primary, fixed color. Printed visuals on the packaging (artwork, icons, fruits, patterns, label graphics) must be preserved exactly as they are, but they should NOT be used to generate a new body color or recolor the product. Meaning: Keep the original product color exactly as it is, and keep the printed elements exactly as they are — but do not use those printed elements as a reason to recolor the product.
- MULTI-PRODUCT INDEPENDENCE: When multiple products are uploaded, keep each product’s original color exactly as it is. Do NOT harmonize, unify, adjust, or change the colors of any product to match the others. Each product keeps its own color independently.
- COLOR & MOOD: You ARE allowed to use the style reference to influence the color mood and overall color grading of the scene and products (e.g. warmer, cooler, more saturated), as long as the original design, flavor, and branding of each product remain clearly recognizable and unchanged.
- CREATIVE SCOPE: Use the reference for environment, lighting, mood, effects, composition, and overall color atmosphere. All creative work should happen AROUND the products and through global grading, not by repainting the packaging.
- RETOUCHING: External retouching effects (lighting, reflections, highlights, shadows, water droplets, atmosphere) are allowed ON TOP of the product, but never inside or replacing its design.
- POSITION & GROUNDING: Always match the product’s physical position in the style reference. If the reference shows the product touching the ground, surface, or table, keep the product grounded with a proper shadow and contact lighting. Do NOT make the product float unless the reference itself shows the product floating. Floating fruits, effects, or particles in the reference do NOT mean the product should float — only the secondary elements may move.
    `;

    // Add the User Prompt (Style description or manual prompt) + System Rules
    const fullPrompt = `${prompt}\n\n${systemRules}`;

    parts.push({ text: fullPrompt });

    const response = await ai.models.generateContent({
      model: 'gemini-2.5-flash-image', // Nano Banana
      contents: { parts },
      config: {
        imageConfig: {
          aspectRatio: aspectRatio,
        },
      },
    });

    // Check for inline data (the image)
    for (const part of response.candidates?.[0]?.content?.parts || []) {
      if (part.inlineData) {
        return `data:image/png;base64,${part.inlineData.data}`;
      }
    }

    throw new Error("No image data found in response");

  } catch (error) {
    console.error("Error generating image:", error);
    throw error;
  }
};

/**
 * Helper to convert Blob/File to Base64 string (without data prefix for API usage if needed, 
 * but @google/genai usually takes raw base64).
 * We will return the raw base64 string.
 */
export const fileToBase64 = (file: File): Promise<string> => {
  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    const reader = new FileReader();
    reader.readAsDataURL(file);
    reader.onload = () => {
      const result = reader.result as string;
      // Remove the data URL prefix (e.g., "data:image/jpeg;base64,")
      const base64 = result.split(',')[1];
      resolve(base64);
    };
    reader.onerror = (error) => reject(error);
  });
};

