    const activePerspective = perspective === CameraPerspective.AUTO 
      ? (inferredPerspective ? `${inferredPerspective} (Inferred)` : "Eye Level (Default)")
      : perspective;

    const activeAspectRatio = aspectRatio === AspectRatio.AUTO ? "1:1" : aspectRatio;

    // 2. The Fixed Base Prompt with Dynamic Values
    const baseRules = `[ SYSTEM OPERATIONAL FOUNDATION ]
----------------------------------------------------------------------
Rely on the following rules and instructions as a core internal operational foundation of the tool.
Build the system’s analysis, generation, and decision-making logic based entirely on these rules, treating them as part of the system’s fundamental structure rather than optional guidance.
The system must reference and depend on these rules throughout all stages of image analysis and final output generation.

[ TECHNICAL CONFIGURATION ]
----------------------------------------------------------------------
Lighting Style:   ${activeLighting}
Camera Angle:     ${activePerspective}
Aspect Ratio:     ${activeAspectRatio}

[ CORE VISUAL DIRECTIVES ]
----------------------------------------------------------------------
• Generate a photorealistic, high-end product photograph.
• Subject: The product is featured in the provided image. Keep it completely unaltered.
• Style: Clean, modern, and professional.

[ INPUT HANDLING & SCENE LOGIC ]
----------------------------------------------------------------------
• PRODUCT IMAGE CONTENT: If the uploaded product image contains people, they are explicitly ALLOWED. The system must operate normally, integrating them into the scene.
• NO REFERENCE IMAGE: If no style reference image is provided, the generation must rely ENTIRELY on the text prompt/rules.
• MANUAL PROMPT PRIORITY: If the user writes a manual prompt, it dictates the scene logic. People are allowed in the result if requested by the prompt or present in the product image, without requiring a reference image.

[ PEOPLE & CHARACTER HANDLING ]
----------------------------------------------------------------------
• PERMISSION: The presence of people in product or reference images is fully permitted.
• DIFFERENT CHARACTER RULE (WITH REFERENCE): If a reference image is used and contains a person, generate a result that follows the reference style but uses a COMPLETELY DIFFERENT character. Do NOT copy the original identity.
• NO REFERENCE SCENARIO: If no reference is provided, generate the scene based on the prompt. If the product image contains a person, they can remain or be adapted as the subject within the new environment described by the prompt.
• INTERACTION LOGIC (WITH REFERENCE):
  - Reference shows person holding product -> Generate DIFFERENT character holding UPLOADED product.
  - Reference shows person (no product) -> Use mood/lighting, generate NEW character.
  - Reference shows person (unrelated product) -> Analyze scene, replace with UPLOADED product held by NEW character.

[ COMPOSITION & ENVIRONMENT ]
----------------------------------------------------------------------
• CRITICAL: Preserve the final output dimensions with NO empty white areas.
• Extend the scene naturally (background, ground texture, atmosphere, lighting) to fill the ENTIRE frame from corner to corner.
• There must be ZERO white space, borders, or padding in the final result.
• Seamlessly integrate all subjects into this full-bleed environment.

[ STRICT NEGATIVE CONSTRAINTS ]
----------------------------------------------------------------------
• STRICT REQUIREMENT: The final generated image must be completely free of text, writing, logos, symbols, and watermarks.
• TEXT BAN: Ensure NO letters, NO characters, and NO written language appear anywhere in the scene. Even if the style reference contains text, IGNORE IT.
• OUTPUT: Purely visual pixels with no typography.

[ SUBJECT INTEGRITY & RULES ]
----------------------------------------------------------------------
• COUNT RULE: Use ONLY the ${productImages.length} uploaded product(s). IGNORE the number of products shown in the style reference images.
• PACKAGING PRESERVATION: Treat each product image as a fixed visual object. Keep every product’s packaging design exactly as it is (logo, label layout, graphics, typography, and key brand colors).
• TRUE COLOR PRESERVATION: Do NOT change or replace the product’s original body color. Always use the real color shown in the uploaded product photo.
• MULTI-PRODUCT INDEPENDENCE: When multiple products are uploaded, keep each product’s original color exactly as it is.

[ CREATIVE EXECUTION ]
----------------------------------------------------------------------
• COLOR & MOOD: Use the style reference (if available) to influence the color mood. If no reference, follow the prompt.
• RETOUCHING: External retouching effects (lighting, reflections, highlights, shadows, water droplets) are allowed ON TOP of the product, but never inside or replacing its design.
• POSITION & GROUNDING: Keep the product grounded with a proper shadow.`;

    // Combine them
